  "result": "I fixed the clamping bug. The full test suite passes (1910 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\n- **Fix:** in `src/click/types.py`, `IntRange._clamp` now returns `bound + dir` instead of `bound - dir`. Clamping with an open (excluded) bound now steps back inside the range. For example, `IntRange(0, 5, min_open=True, clamp=True)` given `-3` now returns `1` instead of `-1`.\n- **Tests:** I added four open-bound clamp cases to `tests/test_types.py`, covering `min_open`, `max_open`, and both together. I didn't run them against the old code to confirm they fail there.\n- **Not done:** I skipped the optional `CHANGES.rst` entry.",
